WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.010
Let's make A spring nature crown.

2
00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:06.840
Arrange fallen leaves on a paper band for a crown full of spring colour.

3
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.940
An adult fits the band and helps with the joins.

4
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.400
Make this project with a grown-up.

5
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.510
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

6
00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:18.135
Pause whenever you need more time.

7
00:00:18.515 --> 00:00:22.680
An adult checks plants, fits the band and removes sharp stems.

8
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:27.595
Wear only while sitting or standing calmly; take it off before active play.

9
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.190
Step 1.

10
00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:31.615
Make a band.

11
00:00:31.995 --> 00:00:35.920
Lay the two card strips end to end with a 3 centimetres overlap.

12
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.440
Tape both sides of the overlap.

13
00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.675
Keep the band flat until the leaves are attached.

14
00:00:42.055 --> 00:00:43.435
Grown-up help.

15
00:00:43.815 --> 00:00:46.670
Prepare the strips and help secure the overlap.

16
00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:49.347
Step 2.

17
00:00:49.727 --> 00:00:51.552
Try a leafy pattern.

18
00:00:51.932 --> 00:00:54.547
Lay six to eight leaves along the band.

19
00:00:54.927 --> 00:00:58.772
Let leaf tips point upward and keep all stems within the card width.

20
00:00:59.152 --> 00:01:01.852
Leave 5 centimetres clear at both ends.

21
00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:04.679
Step 3.

22
00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:06.434
Tape each stem.

23
00:01:06.814 --> 00:01:08.834
Lift one leaf at a time.

24
00:01:09.214 --> 00:01:12.942
Put a short tape strip across its stem and onto the card, then add

25
00:01:12.942 --> 00:01:14.539
a second strip if it moves.

26
00:01:14.919 --> 00:01:17.474
Add the optional flowers the same way.

27
00:01:17.854 --> 00:01:19.234
Grown-up help.

28
00:01:19.614 --> 00:01:23.394
Attach pieces for younger makers and cover any stiff stem ends.

29
00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:25.984
Step 4.

30
00:01:26.364 --> 00:01:27.434
Check the fit.

31
00:01:27.814 --> 00:01:32.216
An adult loosely wraps the band around the maker’s head, overlaps the plain ends

32
00:01:32.216 --> 00:01:33.474
and marks the fit.

33
00:01:33.854 --> 00:01:37.504
Remove it, then tape the overlap inside and outside.

34
00:01:37.884 --> 00:01:39.264
Grown-up help.

35
00:01:39.644 --> 00:01:42.944
Fit and close the crown without pinching hair or skin.

36
00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:45.509
Step 5.

37
00:01:45.889 --> 00:01:47.929
Meet your woodland character.

38
00:01:48.309 --> 00:01:51.714
Put the crown on for a short, supervised moment.

39
00:01:52.094 --> 00:01:56.640
Give it a name, admire the pattern and take it off before running, climbing

40
00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:57.289
or resting.

41
00:01:57.669 --> 00:01:59.049
Grown-up help.

42
00:01:59.429 --> 00:02:03.009
Check for loose leaves and take the crown off for active play.

43
00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:07.416
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

44
00:02:07.796 --> 00:02:11.346
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

45
00:02:11.726 --> 00:02:13.746
Your creation can look different.

46
00:02:14.126 --> 00:02:19.826
Remove tape, reuse or sort the card, and dispose of natural pieces appropriately.

47
00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.411
Display flat on a dry shelf.

48
00:02:22.791 --> 00:02:25.221
Leaves will curl and change colour.

49
00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:26.591
Well done.

50
00:02:26.971 --> 00:02:29.401
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

